# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime and research artifacts
#
# The block above enumerates runtime JSON file-by-file, so every file created
# after that list was written stays visible to git. Today that is 26 untracked
# runtime JSON files; a bare `git add .` would sweep them into a commit.
# The pattern below closes that gap by default-denying runtime JSON in data/
# and re-including the one structural file that is genuinely versioned.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# All runtime JSON in data/ is auto-generated. Default-deny, then re-include
# the single structural file. Order matters: the negation must follow the
# pattern, and data/ itself is never excluded, so the negation can take effect.
data/*.json
!data/donna_settings.json

# Dashboard/debug scratch artifacts written into data/ by ad-hoc checks.
# Deliberately narrow: only leading-underscore files, only these two
# extensions, only directly inside data/ -- never ordinary source.
data/_*.js
data/_*.html

# Raw third-party transcripts: full verbatim source material held locally
# pending Pedro's copyright policy decision. Derived summaries and analysis
# under nova_knowledge_core/ remain tracked -- only the raw capture is hidden.
nova_knowledge_core/TRANSCRIPTS_RAW/
